WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.552
The saved Weekend 10 outline places capacity, informed consent, refusal, de-escalation, severe agitation, prone-positioning hazards, monitoring and palliative issues into class practice. This lesson converts those objectives into original rehearsal cases.
学校保存的第10周纲要将决定能力、知情同意、拒绝、降级沟通、严重躁动、俯卧体位风险、监测及姑息问题纳入课堂实践。本课将这些目标转化为原创排练情景。

00:00:18.552 --> 00:00:30.840
These are practice prompts, not school assessment answers. Perform skills, role-play and any physical procedure only under the instructor’s supervision and the school’s competency requirements.
这些是练习提示，不是学校考核答案。技能、角色扮演和任何身体操作都只能在教师监督及学校能力标准下进行。

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:46.368
Set up a learner, partner and observer. Use the original cases already introduced in this lesson. The observer reveals the next change only after the learner has stated the current plan, so the exercise tests updating rather than hindsight.
设置学员、搭档及观察者，使用本课已介绍的原创案例。学员说出当前计划后，观察者才揭示下一变化，练习因此检验更新能力，而不是事后判断。

00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:58.944
Start with roles, safety, immediate assessment and permission for the proposed interaction. Speak the plan to the patient rather than presenting a monologue to the examiner while ignoring the person.
从角色、安全、即时评估及拟进行互动的许可开始。应对患者说明计划，而不是忽视本人、只对考官长篇陈述。

00:00:58.944 --> 00:01:13.392
Assign one task with an expected report, then use the report to revise the plan. If a necessary finding is missing, ask for it or state the limit; do not have the observer supply a normal result to make the script easier.
每次分派一项任务并说明预期报告，再据此修订计划。缺少必要发现时，应询问或说明局限；不能让观察者补一个正常结果，使台词更容易完成。

00:01:13.392 --> 00:01:24.024
Use the school rubric if available. This original structure is a learning aid, not an invented marking scheme or a substitute for supervised skill assessment.
若有学校评分表，应使用该表。本原创结构是学习辅助，不是自行发明的评分方案，也不替代受监督技能评估。

00:01:24.024 --> 00:01:37.848
British Columbia’s Health Care Consent and Care Facility Admission Act presumes an adult capable unless the applicable legal test is not met. The test is tied to the decision, not to whether the clinician agrees with the choice.
BC《医疗同意及护理机构入院法》推定成年人具备决定能力，除非不符合适用法律标准。判断针对具体决定，不取决于医护人员是否赞同患者选择。

00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:57.288
A diagnosis, intoxication, distress, disability or communication difference does not by itself settle capacity. Section Seven concerns understanding the proposed-care information and understanding that it applies to this adult’s situation; section Eight requires appropriate communication.
诊断、醉酒、痛苦、残疾或沟通差异，单独都不能决定能力。第7条关注理解所提出照护的信息，并理解该信息适用于本人处境；第8条要求适当沟通。

00:01:57.288 --> 00:02:09.720
The school asks learners to explore Understanding, Appreciation, Reasoning and Communication. Use these as prompts to elicit the person’s own account and identify support needs.
学校要求使用理解、领会、推理与沟通四个领域探索。应把它们作为提示，了解患者本人的解释并发现支持需求。

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:29.064
The four domains are not a statutory score. Section Seven asks about the information specified in section Six, paragraph E, and its application to the adult’s own situation. Discuss risks and alternatives, but do not misquote the Act as a separate foreseeable-consequences formula.
四领域不是法定评分。第7条要求理解第6条(e)所列信息及其对本人处境的适用。应讨论风险及替代方案，但不能把法律误引成独立的“可预见后果”公式。

00:02:29.064 --> 00:02:40.416
Use plain language and an interpreter or communication aid when needed. Give the person time when the clinical situation allows, invite questions and avoid arguing or threatening.
需要时使用通俗语言、口译或沟通辅助。临床情况允许时给患者时间，邀请提问，避免争辩或威胁。

00:02:40.416 --> 00:02:57.288
If the patient continues to refuse, follow current BCEHS A09 and local service direction. Consultation may be required. A capable adult may refuse for reasons the clinician would not choose, including where serious consequences are foreseeable.
若患者继续拒绝，应遵循BCEHS现行A09及本地服务指引，并按要求咨询。具备能力的成年人可以因医护人员不认同的理由拒绝，包括可能导致严重后果的情况。

00:02:57.288 --> 00:03:11.232
Name the specific proposal and what was explained. A refusal of transport is not a refusal of every examination, and an agreement to one observation is not agreement to all future interventions.
指出具体提议及所解释内容。拒绝转运不等于拒绝全部检查；同意一项观察也不等于同意以后全部干预。

00:03:11.232 --> 00:03:24.696
Record the communication support and its effect. If an interpreter or hearing support was unavailable, document that limit and what was done next rather than making the record read as though communication was complete.
记录沟通支持及其效果。若口译或听力支持不可用，应记录局限及后续行动，不能把记录写成沟通已经完整。

00:03:24.696 --> 00:03:38.472
Use relevant patient words and observed responses to show the reasoning. Separate the patient’s fear from your clinical concern, and record uncertainty honestly instead of converting disagreement into incapacity.
以相关原话及观察反应体现推理。区分患者恐惧与自己的临床担忧，并诚实记录不确定性，不能把意见不同变成缺乏决定能力。

00:03:38.472 --> 00:03:51.408
Close with the actual plan, required consultation and follow-up responsibility. A signature and a phone number cannot repair missing assessment or a contingency that the person cannot use.
结束时记录实际计划、必需咨询及后续责任。签名及一个号码，不能弥补缺失评估或本人无法使用的应变安排。

00:03:51.408 --> 00:04:04.464
A 74-year-old is found by a building caretaker after a fall. The patient answers questions but repeats one question, reports a headache and declines transport because hospitals feel frightening.
一位74岁患者跌倒后被楼宇管理员发现。患者能回答问题但反复问同一件事，表示头痛，并因害怕医院而拒绝转运。

00:04:04.464 --> 00:04:24.696
Do not use orientation alone as a capacity shortcut. Assess injury and medical threats, explain the concern and recommendation, ask the patient to describe options and likely consequences, address the fear and communication needs, consult the current pathway, and document the person’s own choice.
不要只靠定向力作决定能力捷径。应评估损伤及医学威胁，说明担忧与建议，请患者描述选项和可能后果，处理恐惧及沟通需要，咨询现行流程，并记录患者本人的选择。

00:04:24.696 --> 00:04:59.472
For a vehicle collision, reconstruct the patient mechanism rather than collecting dramatic scenery. Establish which vehicle and position, number and type of vehicles, reported speed, exterior damage and intrusion, restraints/airbags, initial patient condition and any loss of consciousness. Ask about other occupants and a death in the same vehicle when relevant. Record whether a fact is reported, witnessed or directly seen; vehicle damage alone neither diagnoses an injury nor rules one out.
车辆碰撞病史应重建患者机制，不是只收集戏剧性场景。要确定车辆及患者位置、车辆数量类型、报告速度、外部损坏和侵入、安全带气囊、最初状态及是否失去意识；相关时询问其他乘员及同车死亡。注明信息是报告、目击还是亲见，车辆损坏本身既不诊断也不排除损伤。

00:04:59.472 --> 00:05:33.408
For penetrating trauma, the card asks about firearm/type, range, angle and ammunition if known, or an object size and whether a wound was a slash or stab. Include wound number, possible entrances/exits, other injuries, initial condition and consciousness. Scene safety comes first. Do not delay treatment to recover a weapon, probe a wound or invent a bullet trajectory; state uncertainty and avoid assuming the visible wound count proves the number or path of injuries.
穿透伤卡要求已知时询问枪械类型、距离、角度及弹药，或物体尺寸、伤口属划切还是刺入；还包括伤口数、可能入口出口、其他损伤、最初状态和意识。先保证场景安全；不能为找凶器、探伤口或虚构弹道而延误治疗，也不能以可见伤口数证明损伤数量或路径。

00:05:33.408 --> 00:05:49.464
Return to the seventy-four-year-old after the bathroom fall. Begin by acknowledging that hospital feels frightening, then clarify whether the patient is declining transport, an examination, a particular procedure or all contact. These are different decisions.
回到浴室跌倒后的74岁患者。先承认医院令人害怕，再澄清其拒绝的是转运、检查、某项操作，还是全部接触。这些是不同决定。

00:05:49.464 --> 00:06:03.720
An original explanation is: The headache and repeated question after the fall concern me. I cannot rule out an important injury here, and I recommend further assessment. What is the hardest part of that plan for you?
原创解释可以是：“跌倒后的头痛及反复提问让我担心。我在这里不能排除重要损伤，建议进一步评估。这个计划中，哪部分对你最困难？”

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:16.512
Allow the answer, then explain appropriate options without guaranteeing that every test or destination can be chosen. Ask the patient to describe the concern and what the proposed plan means for them.
留出回答时间，再解释适当选项，但不能保证每项检查或目的地都能任意选择。应请患者说明担忧，以及该计划对本人意味着什么。

00:06:16.512 --> 00:06:29.280
Do not use one correct orientation answer as the conclusion. Keep assessing injury and clinical change while supporting the conversation; a fluent sentence does not erase the repeated-question finding.
不能因一个定向力问题答对就作结论。支持对话的同时，应继续评估损伤及临床变化；一句流畅回答不能抹去反复提问这个发现。

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:47.856
For the first original update, reduce noise and provide the preferred communication support. The patient then describes the head-injury concern, explains how the recommendation relates to them and gives a consistent reason for their choice. Record that evidence rather than merely writing capacity confirmed.
第一项原创变化：减少噪声并提供偏好沟通支持后，患者能描述头伤担忧、解释建议如何与本人相关，并为选择给出一致理由。应记录这些证据，而不只写“决定能力已确认”。

00:06:47.856 --> 00:07:03.264
For the second update, the same question continues and the patient cannot demonstrate understanding after appropriate support. That is an unresolved assessment concern, not a reason to pretend an informed refusal has been established.
第二项变化：适当支持后仍反复提问，且不能表现出理解。这是未解决的评估担忧，不能假装已经建立知情拒绝。

00:07:03.264 --> 00:07:17.136
In either version, use the actual current legal and service pathway and obtain indicated consultation. Do not turn the exercise into a universal rule to force transport or to leave every patient who says no.
两种版本都应使用真实现行法律及机构流程，并取得所需咨询。不能把练习变为一概强制转运，或对每位说不者都离开的规则。

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:31.920
If responsiveness or another immediate clinical finding worsens, return to the urgent assessment and explain the change. The previous conversation is evidence about its time, not a permanent clearance for the rest of the encounter.
若反应性或其他即时临床发现恶化，应返回紧急评估并解释变化。先前对话只能证明当时情况，不是本次接触余下时间的永久放行。

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:58.896
The Wednesday outline specifically connects refusal after a seizure with family concern about a changed baseline. The fall case teaches a transferable method, but it does not replace this preparation. In this original rehearsal, an adult has stopped convulsing, pulls away from a crowded doorway and says, I am fine; leave. The partner says the person normally explains their own seizure plan clearly.
周三纲要明确把发作后拒绝与家属报告基线改变联系起来。跌倒案例教的是可迁移方法，但不能替代这项准备。原创排练中，一名成年人抽搐已停止，在拥挤门口躲开众人，说“我没事，走开”；搭档报告，此人平常能清楚解释自己的癫痫照护计划。

00:07:58.896 --> 00:08:25.872
Begin with a calm introduction and space when safe. An original opening is: I can see you want room. May I explain why we are concerned, and what assessment you would accept? Assign the partner a specific clinical task. Consider ongoing recovery, oxygenation, glucose and injury rather than assuming a psychiatric cause; immediate breathing danger takes priority over finishing the conversation.
安全时先冷静介绍身份并留出空间。原创开场可说：“我知道你想要空间。我能解释我们为何担心，以及问问你愿意接受哪些评估吗？”向搭档分派具体临床任务。考虑发作后恢复、氧合、血糖及损伤，而不是假定精神病因；即时呼吸危险优先于完成对话。

00:08:25.872 --> 00:08:57.360
Use the school four-domain prompts to hear the person explain the concern, its relevance, options and choice; apply the distinct legal standard already taught. Reveal an update: after communication support, the person still cannot retain what was explained. Record the actual responses and unresolved risk, reassess and consult through the current pathway. Neither the word postictal nor a family request alone authorizes force or establishes an informed refusal.
用学校四领域提示，听患者解释担忧、对本人的意义、选项及选择；同时应用前文单独教授的法律标准。揭示变化：提供沟通支持后，患者仍无法保留刚解释的信息。记录真实回答及未解决风险，复评并通过现行流程咨询。“发作后”这个词或家属要求，单独都不能授权强制行动，也不能确立知情拒绝。

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:34.704
Original documentation example: at thirteen twenty, a seated older adult has a right-arm pressure of one hundred forty-six over eighty-four and pulse seventy-six. At thirteen twenty-six, after moving to a chair, the left-arm pressure is one hundred thirty-two over eighty and pulse eighty-two. At thirteen thirty, after supported rest, the right-arm pressure is one hundred forty over eighty-two and pulse seventy-eight. Record all three separately, including the arm and movement. The lower left-arm value should not replace the other observations.
原创记录例：13:20，坐位老年患者右臂146/84、脉搏76；13:26，移动至椅子后，左臂132/80、脉搏82；13:30，有支撑休息后，右臂140/82、脉搏78。三组应分别记录，包括手臂及移动。较低左臂值不能替代其他观察。

00:09:34.704 --> 00:10:07.128
Worked interpretation: the arm and activity changed, so the three pressures are not a clean same-condition sequence. Check symptoms, perfusion and technique, then repeat under comparable conditions when appropriate. Do not average away the switch or diagnose recovery from the lowest number. If the person becomes newly confused or breathless, act on that change instead of repeating measurements until one looks reassuring. A precise record makes the uncertainty visible to the next clinician.
推理示范：手臂和活动都变了，三次血压不是条件完全相同的序列。应检查症状、灌注和技术，适当时在可比条件复测；不能靠平均数抹掉换臂，也不能从最低值诊断恢复。若患者新混乱或气短，要处理此变化，不能不停重测直到出现安心数值。精确记录可把不确定性传给下一位临床人员。

00:10:07.128 --> 00:10:21.072
A worker in a poorly ventilated workshop becomes increasingly restless, removes protective clothing and cannot answer a familiar coworker. The temperature is high and a machine remains running.
一名工人在通风不良的车间逐渐躁动，脱掉防护服，无法回答熟悉同事的问题。现场温度很高，机器仍在运行。

00:10:21.072 --> 00:10:40.872
Treat the change as a possible medical emergency, not as a label. Keep responders out of uncontrolled hazards, create space, use one calm speaker, arrange appropriate support and assess airway, breathing, temperature, glucose risk, injury and exposures as safely possible.
应把变化视为可能的医学急症，而不是贴标签。救援人员应避开未控制危险，创造空间，由一名冷静人员沟通，安排适当支援，并在安全范围内评估气道、呼吸、体温、血糖风险、损伤及暴露。

00:10:40.872 --> 00:11:09.408
Start with one connected chain rather than a list of brain parts. A receptor detects a change, neural pathways transmit it, networks integrate it with other information, and muscles or glands produce a response. Central versus peripheral is an anatomical map; sensory, integrative and motor are functional descriptions that cross that boundary. A problem at several different points can change the same visible behavior.
先看一个连贯链条，不只背脑部清单：受体检测变化，神经通路传递，网络结合其他资料整合，再由肌肉腺体产生反应。中枢与周围是解剖地图，感觉整合运动是跨越边界的功能描述。不同位置的问题都可改变同一种可见行为。

00:11:09.408 --> 00:11:37.872
Glia maintain the environment, myelin supports conduction, and circulation and metabolism support the whole system. Therefore, a new difficulty speaking, following a task or moving needs a physiological assessment as well as respectful communication. It does not prove a psychiatric cause, a damaged single brain region or lack of decision-making capacity. Establish what changed from this person's baseline and what could interfere with testing.
胶质维持环境，髓鞘支持传导，循环代谢支持全系统。因此新出现说话、执行任务或动作困难，既需尊重沟通，也需生理评估；不能据此证明精神科病因、单个脑区损坏或缺乏决定能力。先查相对本人基线变了什么、什么会干扰测试。

00:11:37.872 --> 00:12:09.600
The original diagram models a neuronal membrane, not a cardiac monitor trace. The book uses minus seventy millivolts at rest, minus fifty-five near threshold and plus thirty at the peak. These are example values. Sufficient input triggers regenerative sodium entry; sodium-channel inactivation and delayed potassium current then produce repolarization and an afterhyperpolarization. The pump maintains gradients rather than directly making every fast falling phase.
原创图模拟神经元膜，不是心脏监护曲线。书用静息负七十毫伏、阈值附近负五十五、峰值正三十作示例。足够输入触发再生性钠内流；钠通道失活和延迟钾电流随后产生复极及后超极化。泵维持梯度，不直接产生每次快速下降相。

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:39.000
In this model, stronger input generally changes firing frequency or recruitment, not the height of each spike in direct proportion. Myelin lets local current spread between nodes where spikes regenerate; a single sodium ion does not travel from brain to toe. Explain the mechanism without turning the example voltage into a patient threshold or assuming every cell has the same waveform. A change of one hundred millivolts is point one volt.
模型中，更强输入通常改变放电频率或募集，不是让每个尖峰按比例更高。髓鞘让局部电流在结间扩散，尖峰在结处再生；不是一个钠离子从脑走到脚。解释机制时，不能把示例电压当成患者阈值，也不能假定所有细胞波形一样。一百毫伏变化等于零点一伏。

00:12:39.000 --> 00:13:10.704
At a chemical synapse, terminal calcium entry helps release transmitter from vesicles. The transmitter crosses a short cleft and acts through receptors on a target cell. Some receptors directly control channels; others use intracellular signaling. The same transmitter can have different effects at different receptor types. Glutamate, GABA, acetylcholine, amines and peptides are not interchangeable chemicals, and their names alone do not predict the whole patient's behavior.
化学突触中，末端钙内流帮助囊泡释放递质，递质越过短间隙，作用于靶细胞受体。有些受体直接控制通道，另一些用细胞内信号。同一递质在不同受体可有不同作用。谷氨酸、GABA、乙酰胆碱、胺及肽不是可互换化学物，也不能只凭名称预测整位患者行为。

00:13:10.704 --> 00:13:43.080
Separate the switching and effector steps. A G protein uses GDP and GTP cycling; the source caption that says ATP here is inconsistent with its body. An effector such as adenylyl cyclase can separately use ATP to make cyclic AMP. Drugs can affect release, receptors or clearance, but a classroom mechanism does not identify a patient's transmitter level or authorize a sedative. Connect exposure timing to observed physiology and the actual clinical pathway.
区分开关与效应器步骤。G蛋白使用GDP和GTP循环；来源图注在此写ATP，与正文不一致。腺苷酸环化酶等效应器可另外用ATP制造环磷酸腺苷。药物可影响释放受体或清除，但课堂机制不能测出患者递质水平，也不授权镇静药。应把暴露时序与实测生理及实际临床路径连接。

00:13:43.080 --> 00:14:11.592
The assigned neurological chapter organizes examination into mental status, cranial nerves, sensation, motor function and coordination, with gait often listed separately. These are linked samples of function. A problem understanding a command can affect a movement test even if the muscle can work; pain or poor vision can also distort a result. Check the task, baseline and conditions rather than diagnosing from a single failed item.
指定神经章节把检查分为精神状态、脑神经、感觉、运动及协调，步态也常单列。这些是相连功能的抽查。即使肌肉可工作，听不懂指令也可影响动作测试；疼痛或视力差也会干扰。核查任务、基线和条件，不从单项失败下诊断。

00:14:11.592 --> 00:14:42.168
The neurological mental-status examination overlaps with, but is not identical to, the psychiatric mental-state examination. Neither is the legal capacity test. New focal findings, reduced responsiveness or an acute change still need urgent medical assessment. A rapid screen directs the next action; completing every classroom test must not delay support or time-sensitive conveyance. State what was safely examined and what remains uncertain.
神经精神状态检查与精神科精神状态检查重叠但不同，两者都不是法律决定能力测试。新局灶发现、反应下降或急性变化仍需紧急医学评估。快速筛查指引下一行动，不能为做完课堂全部测试延误支持或时间敏感转运。说明安全查过什么、还不确定什么。

00:14:42.168 --> 00:15:12.216
Before calling a response abnormal, make the question accessible. Reduce noise, check hearing and language needs, and explain one appropriate task. Then distinguish language comprehension or production from motor articulation. Someone can speak fluently without understanding, or understand while struggling to produce words. A familiar accent, a word-list score or a nod is not enough to settle either neurological function or consent.
宣布反应异常前，先让问题可理解：降噪，查听力语言需要，说明一个恰当任务。再区分语言理解产生与运动构音。人可说得流利却不理解，也可理解却难产词。熟悉口音、词表分数或点头，都不足以决定神经功能或同意。

00:15:12.216 --> 00:15:40.896
If new naming difficulty or an asymmetric movement persists after communication support, do not explain it away as stress. Establish timing and baseline, compare the other domains and assess immediate threats. The reading's classical language areas help explain networks, but do not give a precise lesion diagnosis from one answer. Ask whether the finding changes urgency, what support is needed and what the receiving clinician must know.
沟通支持后若新命名困难或不对称动作仍存在，不能用压力解释掉。明确时序基线，比较其他领域，检查即时威胁。阅读中的经典语言区帮助解释网络，不能从一个回答精确诊断病灶。应问该发现如何改变紧迫性，需要何支持，接收者必须知道什么。

00:15:40.896 --> 00:16:11.616
Keep the functions separate. Detecting a peripheral object while holding fixation tests a field; following a target tests eye movement. Pupillary light response involves optic input, bilateral central connections and oculomotor parasympathetic output. Compare the observation with drugs, prior eye problems and other findings. The textbook's optic nerve versus tract naming does not make the chiasm a peripheral-to-central border; the optic nerve is CNS-derived too.
功能要分开：保持注视时察觉周边物体查视野，跟随目标查眼球运动。瞳孔对光涉及视神经输入、双侧中枢连接及动眼副交感输出。结合药物、既往眼病及其他发现解释。教材视神经与视束名称不使视交叉变成周围到中枢边界，视神经本身也属中枢来源。

00:16:11.616 --> 00:16:43.848
Source corrections also matter: the sixth-nerve nucleus is pontine, and an MLF-related internuclear pattern primarily impairs adduction, not simply abduction. In the field, report the actual movement and associated deficits rather than pretending the cause is certain. Do not force head rotation, neck resistance or a gag response in an unsafe context. A normal-looking single pupil or gaze observation does not rule out every serious neurological cause.
来源纠错也重要：第六脑神经核在脑桥，MLF相关核间性模式主要影响内收，不只是外展。院前应报告实际动作及伴随缺损，不假装病因确定。不安全背景下不能强转头、颈抗阻或诱发咽反射。单个瞳孔注视看似正常，也不排除所有严重神经病因。

00:16:43.848 --> 00:17:13.392
Compare meaningful sensory and motor findings across sides, using the actual trained method and safe equipment. An arm that pronates and drifts is an abnormal observation, not the reassuring negative result mistakenly described in one source sentence. Tone, reflexes and strength form patterns with important timing and injury limits. Do not diagnose a cord level from one point or use an improvised sharp implement to complete a chart.
按真实受训方法和安全器材比较有意义的左右感觉运动发现。手臂旋前下漂是异常，不是来源一句误写的放心阴性结果。张力、反射、力量构成模式，但有重要时序伤情限制。不能凭一点诊断脊髓平面，也不用临时尖物完成表格。

00:17:13.392 --> 00:17:44.736
Coordination depends on sensory feedback, vision, motor output and cerebellar connections. Ataxia can have central, peripheral, toxic or metabolic explanations; it does not prove intoxication. If the person is already unstable or injured, observe safely and document why a gait task was not attempted. Do not demand tandem walking, hopping or a push to prove abnormality, and do not mistake a normal single task for a complete exclusion of stroke.
协调依赖感觉反馈、视觉、运动输出及小脑连接。共济失调可有中枢、周围、毒性或代谢解释，不证明醉酒。患者已不稳或受伤时，安全观察并说明为何未做步态任务。不能要求走直线、单脚跳或推搡来证明异常，也不能把单项正常当成完全排除卒中。

00:17:44.736 --> 00:18:14.280
In this original case, a fifty-four-year-old mechanic is described as stressed after an argument. You reduce workshop noise and clarify hearing and language needs. New naming difficulty and right-arm drift remain. Family report a normal baseline at twelve ten, and the simulation gives a measured glucose of six point two millimoles per litre. Those findings are not explained away by emotion or by one glucose in a usual range.
本原创案例中，五十四岁技师争执后被说成压力大。你降低车间噪声并澄清听力语言需要，但新命名困难和右臂漂移仍存在。家属报告十二点十分正常，模拟给实测血糖每升六点二毫摩尔。这些发现不能被情绪或一个通常范围血糖解释掉。

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:48.576
Assess and support immediate threats, record last-known-well and serial findings, and escalate through the applicable stroke pathway. Symptom improvement does not make the episode safe to ignore or prove there was no infarction. Do not import the textbook story's aspirin as an undifferentiated field order. Handover what you measured, what changed after communication support, the times, actions and remaining uncertainty. Neurological findings inform the actual decision; they do not replace the separate consent process.
应评估支持即时威胁，记录最后正常及连续发现，按适用卒中路径升级。症状好转不代表可忽略，也不证明没有梗死。不能把教材故事的阿司匹林套成未分型院前医嘱。交接实测、沟通支持后仍有什么变化、时间、行动及不确定性。神经发现帮助真实决定，不替代独立同意流程。

00:18:48.576 --> 00:19:16.200
In this original cafe rehearsal, a forty-six-year-old repeatedly stands and says the legs cannot stay still after a medication increase. Ask what changed, obtain the actual product and last dose, and examine glucose, vital signs and movement. Akathisia is one possible explanation, not proof of defiance or a final diagnosis. Keep illness, substances and other adverse effects in view.
本原创咖啡馆排练中，一位四十六岁者加药后反复站起，说双腿无法安静。询问变化，获取真实药品及末次量，检查血糖、体征和动作。静坐不能只是可能解释，不证明故意不配合，也不是最终诊断。仍须考虑疾病、物质及其他不良作用。

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:46.392
Now change one feature: fever, marked rigidity and impaired responsiveness appear. That pattern raises concern for a dangerous drug reaction such as neuroleptic malignant syndrome, among other causes. Reassess airway, ventilation and circulation, obtain temperature and timing, and escalate urgently. Do not keep treating a behavioral label while physiology worsens, or convert the textbook specialist-drug examples into a PCP treatment order.
现在改变一项：出现发热、显著僵硬及反应受损。该模式提示恶性综合征等危险药物反应，也有其他病因。重查气道、通气循环，取得体温时序并紧急升级。不能生理恶化还只处理行为标签，也不能把教材专科药物举例变成PCP医嘱。

00:19:46.392 --> 00:20:17.640
In the next variation, recent diarrhea, lithium use and new unsteadiness replace the original medication history. Lithium has a narrow therapeutic margin and renal elimination. Fluid loss, kidney impairment or an interacting medicine can change exposure even when the prescribed dose was followed. Ask about intake, vomiting, urine changes, last dose and medicines such as NSAIDs or diuretics; do not simply call the presentation recurrent mania.
下一变式把原用药史改为近期腹泻、服锂及新步态不稳。锂治疗窗窄，经肾排出。即使遵处方，失液、肾损伤或交互药仍可改变暴露。询问摄入、呕吐、尿量改变、末次量及NSAIDs利尿剂等药，不能只把表现叫躁狂复发。

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:47.808
Assess the actual patient and support immediate threats while obtaining appropriate clinical help. A prescribed milligram dose is not a serum concentration, and the textbook toxicity bands are not guaranteed symptom stages. Do not wait for laboratory confirmation before responding to deterioration, force water into an unsafe swallow, or calculate a catch-up dose from a maintenance table. Handover the measured findings, exposure timing and uncertainty.
应评估实际患者，支持即时威胁并获取适当临床帮助。处方毫克量不等于血药浓度，教材中毒分档也不是必然症状阶段。不能恶化还等化验、向吞咽不安全者灌水，或从维持表计算补服量。交接实测发现、暴露时序及不确定性。

00:20:47.808 --> 00:21:19.296
After a sedative exposure, the patient becomes quiet but breathing is slower and shallower. That is not automatically successful de-escalation. Check airway patency, effective ventilation, circulation and responsiveness, compare the trend and provide indicated support. Alcohol, opioids and other depressants can compound the problem. RASS helps describe arousal; it cannot replace respiratory assessment or determine capacity by itself.
镇静暴露后，患者安静了，呼吸却更慢更浅。这不自动表示降级沟通成功。检查气道通畅、有效通气、循环反应，比较趋势并给予有适应证支持。酒精、阿片及其他抑制剂可叠加问题。RASS帮助描述觉醒，不能替代呼吸评估，也不能单独决定能力。

00:21:19.296 --> 00:21:51.048
The reading names flumazenil, but its availability does not replace airway and ventilation support. Reversal can provoke seizures in high-risk circumstances and sedation may recur. Obtain appropriate clinical or toxicology help rather than treating every drowsy person with an assumed antidote. Current G01 places pharmacological restraint under ACP interventions; a nursing dose table or a student lecture does not create PCP administration or reversal authority.
阅读点名氟马西尼，但有此药不替代气道通气支持。高风险背景下逆转可诱发癫痫，镇静也可能复发。应取得适当临床毒理帮助，不能给每位嗜睡者套用假定解毒药。现行G01把药物约束列在ACP干预；护理剂量表或学生课件不产生PCP给药或逆转权限。

00:21:51.048 --> 00:22:20.784
Use this original cook case to connect all three assigned CNS ranges. The forty-seven-year-old has a four-month history of back pain, new abdominal discomfort and tremor after reducing alcohol. A companion answers many questions. These findings need a safe, accessible assessment, not an immediate psychiatric, withdrawal or abuse label. Establish the person's own account, baseline, timing and immediate physiological needs.
用原创厨师案例联系三段CNS阅读。四十七岁者有四个月背痛史，新腹部不适及减酒后手抖，陪同回答许多问题。需要安全可理解评估，不是立即贴精神科、戒断或虐待标签。明确本人说法、基线时序及即时生理需要。

00:22:20.784 --> 00:22:48.216
Set a useful communication goal, make the message understandable, listen, clarify and check the response. Do not treat politeness, a nod or a quiet manner as proof of understanding or comfort. Support the person without promising secrecy or a service you cannot guarantee. The whole reading is communication, pain and psychosocial assessment; its Chapter Twenty is not an end-of-life chapter.
设有用沟通目标、让信息可懂、倾听澄清核实反应。礼貌点头或安静不证明理解舒适。支持本人，不许诺绝对保密或无法保证的服务。整项阅读涉及沟通、痛及社会心理，第20章不是临终章。

00:22:48.216 --> 00:23:15.744
Distinguish pain from nociception. Transduction begins at sensory endings, transmission carries and processes neural activity, perception is the experienced pain, and modulation changes processing through spinal and descending influences. The source's gate model is not a literal valve, and the brain is not consciously choosing a person's pain. An inability to speak does not mean the person cannot experience pain.
区分痛与伤害感受。转换始于感觉末梢，传递运送处理活动，感知是体验疼痛，调制经脊髓下行影响改变处理。来源闸门不是实际阀，脑不是有意识替本人选疼痛。不能说话不表示不会体验痛。

00:23:15.744 --> 00:23:43.992
In the cook case, calm behavior and an ordinary-looking back do not invalidate the pain report. Biological, psychological and social influences can change the experience without making it imaginary. Ask about location, quality, onset, function and associated symptoms. Do not infer severity from apparent injury size or replace assessment with a promise that a positive attitude or rubbing the site will remove the pain.
厨师镇定及背外观普通，不否定痛自述。生物心理社会影响可改变体验，不使它变假。询问部位性质、起病功能及伴随症状。不能凭可见伤大小推强度，也不用积极想或揉一揉保证消痛代替评估。

00:23:43.992 --> 00:24:13.440
The source repeatedly uses six months for chronic pain; current IASP classification uses persistence or recurrence beyond three months. That difference does not make the cook's new abdominal pain part of an established harmless problem. Duration, site, mechanism and intensity are separate axes. Referred pain is felt away from its source; radiation describes spread. Neither a location nor a descriptive word confirms the cause.
来源反复用六个月定义慢痛，现行IASP用持续或反复超过三个月。此差异不使厨师新腹痛成为已知无害问题。时长、部位、机制强度是不同维度。牵涉是在远离来源处感到，放射描述扩散，部位词句都不确诊。

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:42.456
A transient breakthrough flare is different from continuously uncontrolled background pain or a new illness. Neuropathic pain involves a lesion or disease of the somatosensory system; tingling alone does not prove that diagnosis. Diabetic neuropathy is not explained only by reduced circulation. Use these mechanisms to ask better questions and communicate uncertainty, not to select a new drug or invent a rescue dose.
短暂爆发加剧不同于持续未控背景痛或新病。神经病理痛涉及躯体感觉系统病损疾病，麻刺不独立证明；糖尿病神经病变也不只循环减少。用机制改进提问交接不确定性，不据此选新药或编救援量。

00:24:42.456 --> 00:25:10.536
Use a pain tool the person can understand. A number records their reported intensity, not injury severity or an automatic medication dose. Wong-Baker FACES is also self-report: the person selects the face representing their pain. It is not a way to match their expression, measure mood or score an unresponsive person. Use the actual appropriate instructions and do not copy or modify licensed artwork.
用本人能理解的痛工具。数字记录自述强度，不是伤严重度或自动药量。Wong-Baker FACES也属自评，由本人选代表痛的脸，不是匹配表情、测心情或给无反应者评分。使用真实合适指引，不复制修改许可图。

00:25:10.536 --> 00:25:40.416
For an appropriate observational assessment, FLACC has five categories scored zero to two each, so the maximum is ten, not the textbook's twelve. In this original addition exercise, supplied scores of one, zero, one, two and one total five out of ten. The exercise checks arithmetic only. Actual scoring needs the defined criteria, a suitable patient and context; a number does not identify the cause of distress.
适当观察评估中，FLACC五项各零至二，最高十不是教材十二。原创加法给一、零、一、二、一，共五分满十，只查计算。真实评分需规定标准、合适患者背景；数字不辨痛苦病因。

00:25:40.416 --> 00:26:08.952
The source gives sympathetic and parasympathetic changes as pain and relief clues. They are not a pain meter. A normal pulse cannot refute pain; reduced heart rate, small pupils or quietness cannot establish comfortable recovery. With the cook, compare the actual report and function with breathing, responsiveness and other findings. An improved pain score with reduced ventilation is not an uncomplicated success.
来源把交感副交感变化当痛与缓解线索，但不是疼痛计。正常脉不否定痛，心率降、瞳孔小或安静不确定舒适恢复。厨师须把自述功能与呼吸反应等比较。痛分好转却通气降，不是无问题成功。

00:26:08.952 --> 00:26:37.656
Record the tool, time frame, symptoms, goal, intervention and response. Reassess at a time appropriate to the actual route and expected effect, and immediately if deterioration appears. Onset is not the same as duration of action. The assigned opioid table mixes product strengths, patch rates and weight-based quantities; it is not one universal adult dose or permission to repeat a medicine until the number falls.
记录工具、时间框架、症状目标、干预反应。按真实途径预期效果在合适时间复评，恶化立即查。起效不同持续时间。指定阿片表混有产品强度、贴剂速率及按体重量，不是一个成人通量，也不许一直重复到分降。

00:26:37.656 --> 00:27:08.448
Describe mood, affect, speech, motor activity, thought form and content, perception, attention and memory. Mood is more sustained; affect is the observed expression, not a lie detector. Consider baseline, communication, pain, medicines and medical causes. A nod, one correct gesture or orientation to four items is not a legal capacity test or proof that a new cognitive change has no serious cause.
描述心境情感、言语运动、思维形式内容、感知注意记忆。心境较持续，情感是观察表达，不是测谎。结合基线沟通、痛、药及医学病因。点头、单个手势或四项定向，不是法律能力测试，也不证明新认知变无严重病因。

00:27:08.448 --> 00:27:41.256
Ask neutrally about frightening perceptions and actual safety concerns rather than arguing or endorsing an unverified event. Thoughts, intent, plans, access and past behavior are separate parts of a risk assessment. Do not require all of them to be present before taking concern seriously or let protective factors erase it. Use the trained safety, supervision, escalation and accepted-handover process, not an unfamiliar questionnaire as an independent clearance test.
中性问可怕感知及真实安全担忧，不争辩也不认可未核实事件。想法、意图计划、可及性及既往行为是不同风险部分，不能要求全齐才认真，也不能让保护因素抹去担忧。用受训安全监督、升级及接收交接，不用陌生问卷独立放行。

00:27:41.256 --> 00:28:10.848
The cook's tremor after reducing alcohol raises a concern; it does not establish the cause of every symptom. Ask about timing, amount, previous seizures or severe withdrawal, medicines, co-use and other illness. Withdrawal windows overlap and vary. A positive alcohol level neither rules it in nor rules it out, and CIWA-Ar scores can reflect other conditions. Do not wait for a textbook clock before responding to a severe finding.
厨师减酒后抖引起担忧，不确定每个症状原因。问时序量、既往癫痫重戒断、药、合用及其他病。戒断窗口可重叠变化，血酒阳性既不证实也不排除，CIWA-Ar分也可反映其他病。不能等教材时钟才处理严重发现。

00:28:10.848 --> 00:28:43.080
Alcohol and sedative withdrawal can be dangerous, while opioid intoxication may threaten ventilation. Substance-use diagnosis, intoxication and physiological dependence are not interchangeable. Screeners need their actual instructions: the source confuses the single alcohol screening question, SASQ, with the longer dependence questionnaire, SADQ. The nursing drug and withdrawal tables are not medication orders or a reason to disregard the patient's own account.
酒及镇静物戒断可危险，阿片中毒可能威胁通气。物质诊断、中毒及身体依赖不能互换。筛查须真实指引，来源混淆单项SASQ与更长依赖问卷SADQ。护理药戒断表不是医嘱，也不能据此忽视本人说法。

00:28:43.080 --> 00:29:09.264
In a safely private conversation, the cook reports that a partner has threatened them and controls access to medicines. Acknowledge the account and ask about current needs and safety without demanding the whole story. A companion answering earlier was a cue to explore, not proof. Do not confront the partner, announce the disclosure in their presence or use them to interpret a sensitive conversation.
安全私谈时，厨师报告伴侣威胁及控制药物。认可说法、问当前需要安全，不逼全部故事。早先陪同代答是探索线索，不是证明。不能对质伴侣、当其面宣布披露，或让其翻译敏感谈话。

00:29:09.264 --> 00:29:39.744
Consent, medical care, evidence collection and police involvement are different questions. A relationship never creates entitlement to sex, and refusing sex is not itself abuse. Ask what contact or material can be received safely; a shared phone or printed note may be discovered. Follow the actual clinical and safeguarding process while respecting the person's involvement, and document the words, findings, consultation and accepted next step.
同意、医疗、取证及警方参与是不同问题。关系从不产生索取性行为权，拒绝本身不是虐待。问何联系资料能安全接收，共用手机纸条可能被发现。尊重本人参与并依真实临床保护流程，记录词句、发现、咨询及接收下一步。

00:29:39.744 --> 00:30:06.312
Keep the source's American reporting examples separate from BC practice. A child is under nineteen under the BC child-protection Act, and the actual reporting provision includes a specific Indigenous-authority route. Do not import a twelve-hour rule or treat poverty alone as proof. Preserve the relevant words and safety concern; a clinician should not conduct a repeated leading interview to manufacture evidence.
分开来源美国报告例子与BC实践。BC儿童法儿童为十九岁以下，真实报告条款含具体原住民机构路径。不能移植十二小时规则或仅凭贫困认定。保留相关原词安全担忧，临床者不能反复诱导访谈来制造证据。

00:30:06.312 --> 00:30:33.720
Adult safeguarding uses a different framework and may involve a designated agency under specified circumstances. The chapter's broad mandatory-report claim is not a universal BC rule for every older or sexually assaulted adult. Apply the relevant law, service process and consultation to the actual case, rather than guessing authority from age. Immediate threats still require the appropriate safety and clinical response.
成人保护框架不同，特定条件下可涉及指定机构。章节宽泛强制报告说法，不是每位老年或受性侵成人的BC通则。按真实案例用相关法、服务咨询，不凭年龄猜权限。即时威胁仍需恰当安全及临床响应。

00:30:33.720 --> 00:31:00.600
Handover the cook's new symptoms and actual findings, the duration and pattern of pain, recent alcohol reduction and other exposures, and the response to authorized support. Keep the patient's report separate from the companion's account and your hypotheses. A calm appearance does not invalidate pain, a tremor does not settle withdrawal and a disclosure does not remove the need to assess the acute medical problem.
交接厨师新症状真实发现、痛时长模式、近期减酒其他暴露及授权支持反应。分开本人、陪同说法及自己的假设。镇定不否定痛，手抖不确定戒断，披露也不取消评估急性医学问题。

00:31:00.600 --> 00:31:26.736
Confirm who has accepted the next step and communicate privately through the appropriate secure route. Record the person's choices, what remains uncertain and what will happen if the plan fails. Supporting immediate safety is not a promise to solve every social problem. Rehearse again by changing only one fact, such as reduced responsiveness, then explain which priority and clinical pathway must change.
确认谁接收下一步，经恰当安全渠道私下沟通。记录本人选择、未定内容及计划失败怎么办。支持即时安全不等于承诺解决全部社会问题。可只改一事实如反应下降再排练，说明何重点及临床路径须改变。

00:31:26.736 --> 00:31:42.408
The hot workshop combines a changing patient with machinery and a narrow exit. Do not enter an uncontrolled exposure to begin the interview. State the hazard and obtain the appropriate control or assistance before assuming contact is safe.
高温车间把患者变化、机械及狭窄出口叠加在一起。不能为了开始访谈进入未控制暴露。应指出危险，并取得适当控制或协助，不能假定接触安全。

00:31:42.408 --> 00:31:58.248
Assign one lead communicator. Ask the partner for a clear observation or clinical task within the safe plan and request a report. A vague instruction to watch everything does not establish who owns airway observation or exit awareness.
指定一名主要沟通者。在安全计划内向搭档分派明确观察或临床任务，并要求报告。笼统说“什么都看着”，并未确定谁负责气道观察或出口态势。

00:31:58.248 --> 00:32:14.112
Use short, non-threatening communication while assessing the possible medical change. Heat, exposure, injury, glucose disturbance and other causes remain possibilities; do not diagnose from a historical excited-delirium label.
评估可能医学变化时，使用简短而不具威胁性的沟通。热、暴露、损伤、血糖紊乱及其他病因仍是可能性；不能用历史“兴奋性谵妄”标签确诊。

00:32:14.112 --> 00:32:25.368
If specific conduct or the environment becomes unsafe, coordinate withdrawal and support. The goal is safe care, not proving that conversation can solve every scene.
若具体行为或环境变得不安全，应协调撤离及支援。目标是安全照护，不是证明对话能解决所有现场。

00:32:25.368 --> 00:32:51.384
The actual third PMHN range is schizophrenia, not mood disorders. Together the four assigned ranges teach anger and safety, rights, psychotic symptoms, personality patterns and ongoing care. Their content does not itself supply a complete field protocol for the school's historical agitation label. Use the actual school monitoring tasks and current service pathway, while preserving this broader reading.
真实PMHN第三段是精神分裂症，而不是心境障碍。四段合起来教授愤怒与安全、权利、精神病性症状、人格模式及持续照护，但并不提供学校历史性躁动标签下的完整院前规程。应使用真实学校监测任务及现行服务流程，同时完整学习这些更广的阅读内容。

00:32:51.384 --> 00:33:22.080
In this original case, a thirty-two-year-old museum guide has an established schizophrenia diagnosis and a recent prescription change. Today they are pacing, distressed and experiencing jaw pulling. The diagnosis does not establish the cause. Assess current physiology, breathing, responsiveness, exposure timing and other findings, with appropriate urgent help. Do not assume that restlessness means more antipsychotic medication is needed.
原创案例中，一位三十二岁博物馆导览员有既往精神分裂症诊断，最近处方改变。今天出现踱步、痛苦及下颌牵拉。诊断不能确定此次病因。应评估当前生理状态、呼吸、反应、暴露时序及其他发现，并适当紧急求助。不能假设不安就代表需要更多抗精神病药。

00:33:22.080 --> 00:33:51.672
Positive symptoms are abnormally present experiences, not good symptoms. Negative symptoms describe reduced expected function, not bad character. Cognitive difficulties concern attention, memory and using information. Describe what the guide actually says or does and compare with baseline. A quiet expression does not prove comfort, and a new reduction in movement or speech is not automatically a chronic negative symptom.
阳性症状是异常出现的体验，不是好症状；阴性症状是原有功能减少，不是品格不好；认知困难涉及注意、记忆及利用信息。应描述导览员实际言行并与基线比较。表情安静不证明舒适，新发言语或动作减少也不能自动归为慢性阴性症状。

00:33:51.672 --> 00:34:23.712
If a person reports a threatening voice, ask neutrally about the experience, its effect, any command and current safety. Do not argue, ridicule or confirm an unverified event. A command does not guarantee obedience, but a reassuring answer does not complete risk assessment. Psychosis, delirium, a substance effect and schizophrenia are not interchangeable. A normal test or positive toxicology result does not exclude every medical explanation.
若本人报告威胁性的声音，应中性询问体验、影响、是否有命令及当前安全，不争辩、嘲讽或认可未核实事件。命令不保证本人服从，但一句安慰性回答也不能完成风险评估。精神病性症状、谵妄、物质效应及精神分裂症不能互换。正常检查或毒理阳性都不能排除所有医学解释。

00:34:23.712 --> 00:34:55.344
Akathisia can produce distressing restlessness and pacing. Acute dystonia can produce sustained involuntary contractions, while drug-induced parkinsonism and tardive dyskinesia have different patterns. The museum guide's jaw and movement findings need assessment, not a diagnosis by resemblance. Verify the actual drug, formulation, dose history and timing. Do not copy the nursing table's dose changes or treatment choices into an unauthorized field order.
静坐不能可产生痛苦的不安与踱步，急性肌张力障碍可产生持续不自主收缩，药源性帕金森综合征与迟发性运动障碍又有不同模式。导览员的下颌及动作发现需要评估，不能凭外观相似诊断。应核实真实药物、剂型、剂量史及时序，不把护理表中的改量或治疗选择变成未经授权的院前医嘱。

00:34:55.344 --> 00:35:27.744
Relevant medication exposure with hyperthermia, rigidity, altered mental status or autonomic instability raises an emergency concern. Do not wait for exactly two weeks or every classic feature before escalating. Sedation, orthostatic symptoms, anticholinergic effects and other medicines also matter. After authorized care, follow breathing, responsiveness and the actual response; a quieter person does not prove that either the illness or the treatment risk has resolved.
相关用药暴露伴高热、僵硬、精神状态变化或自主神经不稳定，会引起急症担忧。不能等恰好两周或所有典型表现齐全才升级。镇静、体位症状、抗胆碱效应及其他药物也有意义。获授权照护后，应监测呼吸、反应及真实变化；人变安静不证明疾病或治疗风险已消失。

00:35:27.744 --> 00:36:00.144
The source repeatedly treats written consent as the whole process. In BC, consent can be oral, written or inferred from conduct, specific to the care agreed to. Explain the concern, proposed care, relevant risks, benefits and alternatives, and support questions and understanding. Do not infer incapability from schizophrenia, disagreement, distress or one orientation result. The existing school refusal conversation remains an aid, not a statutory score.
来源反复把书面同意当成整个过程。在BC，同意可口头、书面或由行为推定，并限于所同意的照护。应解释担忧、拟议照护、相关风险益处及替代方案，并支持提问与理解。不能从精神分裂症、意见不同、痛苦或一次定向结果推断无能力。现有学校拒绝沟通框架仍只是辅助，不是法定评分。

00:36:00.144 --> 00:36:30.504
An emergency, a substitute decision and a Mental Health Act status require their actual conditions and roles. The source's generic seventy-two-hour hold is not the BC process. Neither a medication order nor a relative's insistence gives unlimited authority. In the guide case, establish what is proposed, the patient's actual decision and the lawful next step, while addressing immediate medical danger and obtaining appropriate consultation.
紧急情况、替代决定及《精神卫生法》状态均需符合真实条件与角色。来源泛称七十二小时扣留，不是BC流程。药物医嘱或亲属坚持都不提供无限权限。在导览员案例中，应明确拟做什么、本人真实决定及合法下一步，同时处理即时医学危险并适当咨询。

00:36:30.504 --> 00:37:03.192
The restraint table mixes renewal, evaluation, monitoring, care and removal. Its American four, two and one-hour figures describe age-based order-renewal limits for violent or self-destructive restraint; the initial face-to-face evaluation is a separate within-one-hour requirement. This corrects the textbook, not a BC field schedule. Do not wait for any maximum time before reassessing, and do not use a renewal limit as permission to continue a harmful intervention.
约束表混合了续开、评估、监测、照护和解除。美国四、二、一小时数字，是暴力或自伤约束按年龄区分的医嘱续开上限；首次面对面评估另有一小时内要求。这是在纠正教材，不提供BC院前时间表。不能等到最长时限才复评，也不能把续开上限当作继续有害干预的许可。

00:37:03.192 --> 00:37:35.976
Seclusion is not simply offering a quiet room that someone can leave. Restriction needs the actual lawful, trained and least-restrictive process, with appropriate assessment, monitoring and review. Do not adopt the source table's prone-position suggestion. The existing school hard stops remain in place. Document behavior and risk, alternatives, authority, intervention and response, and communicate a deterioration immediately rather than reporting only that the person has become calm.
隔离约束不同于提供一个可以自由离开的安静房间。限制需要真实合法、受训且最少限制的流程，并有适当评估、监测和复核。不能采用来源表中的俯卧体位建议，现有学校硬性禁忌仍保留。应记录行为与风险、替代措施、权限、干预和反应；恶化时立即沟通，不能只报告本人变平静。

00:37:35.976 --> 00:38:08.976
The chapter opening names only one example per cluster, but the later pages describe all ten patterns. Cluster A contains paranoid, schizoid and schizotypal; B contains antisocial, borderline, histrionic and narcissistic; C contains avoidant, dependent and obsessive-compulsive personality patterns. Learn their differences in the paired reading. They are longitudinal descriptions, not a way to label a frightened person from one disagreement or decide who deserves care.
章节开头每组只写一个例子，但后文描述十种模式。A组含偏执型、分裂样及分裂型；B组含反社会型、边缘型、表演型及自恋型；C组含回避型、依赖型及强迫型人格模式。应在对照阅读中学习差别。它们是纵向描述，不能凭一次意见不同给惊恐者贴标签，更不能据此决定谁配接受照护。

00:38:08.976 --> 00:38:39.648
Obsessive-compulsive personality disorder is not OCD, and schizoid or schizotypal is not schizophrenia. Conduct disorder does not automatically convert to antisocial personality disorder at eighteen. A diagnosis also does not determine intent, capacity or medical stability. Respect cultural and developmental context, explore functioning and actual support needs, and keep an acute medical change separate from an established personality or psychiatric history.
强迫型人格障碍不等于OCD，分裂样或分裂型人格也不等于精神分裂症。品行障碍不会在十八岁自动转成反社会型人格障碍。诊断也不能决定意图、决定能力或医学稳定性。应尊重文化发育背景、探索功能及真实支持需要，并把急性医学变化与既往人格或精神科病史分开。

00:38:39.648 --> 00:39:09.864
The personality chapter discusses CBT, DBT, practical supports and a collaborative crisis plan. DBT skills include mindfulness, distress tolerance, emotion regulation and interpersonal effectiveness; one brief exercise is not the full treatment. Ask what the person already finds helpful and whether it is safe now. Neither an ice technique, a breathing count nor a diagnostic label guarantees relief or replaces urgent assessment.
人格章节讨论CBT、DBT、实际支持及合作危机计划。DBT技能包括正念、痛苦耐受、情绪调节和人际效能，一次简短练习不是完整治疗。应问本人已发现什么有用，以及现在是否安全。冰冷技巧、呼吸计数或诊断标签都不保证缓解，也不能代替紧急评估。

00:39:09.864 --> 00:39:41.016
Treat self-harm and suicidal concerns as current needs, even if the person has attended before or a chart uses an attention-seeking label. Assess injury, intent, distress and safety without punishment. Do not require a written account before providing necessary care or engaging with the person. Predictable boundaries can coexist with compassion. A promise not to self-harm is not proof of safety or a substitute for an accepted support and supervision plan.
即使本人以前来过，或病历使用“寻求关注”标签，自伤及自杀担忧仍需按当前需要处理。应不带惩罚地评估损伤、意图、痛苦和安全，不能要求先写经过才提供必要照护或与本人交流。可预期界限可以与同情并存。承诺不自伤不证明安全，也不代替已落实的支持和监督计划。

00:39:41.016 --> 00:40:09.912
For the museum guide, hand over the new pacing and jaw findings, medication-change timeline, current examination, the person's own report and the response to authorized support. Distinguish an observation, a hypothesis and a confirmed history. Protect privacy and use appropriate chosen support. Do not let a psychiatric label erase a new medical concern, or let a social or safety concern cancel the clinical assessment.
对博物馆导览员，应交接新发踱步及下颌表现、用药变化时序、当前检查、本人说法及授权支持反应。应区分观察、假设与已确认病史。保护隐私并适当使用本人选择的支持。不能让精神科标签抹去新医学问题，也不能让社会或安全问题取消临床评估。

00:40:09.912 --> 00:40:41.568
Agree a realistic next step and confirm who has accepted it. A useful plan includes what matters to the person, what remains uncertain and what will happen if distress or physiology worsens. Afterwards, review communication, environmental triggers, access barriers and clinician assumptions without blame or identifying informal disclosures. This closes the reading-to-practice loop while leaving formal diagnosis, prescribing and supervised skill assessment with their proper services.
应商定真实可行的下一步并确认谁已接收。有用计划包括本人重视什么、哪些仍未确定，以及痛苦或生理状态恶化怎么办。之后应不责备地复盘沟通、环境诱因、资源障碍及临床假设，避免可识别身份的非正式披露。这将阅读联系到实践，同时把正式诊断、处方及受监督技能考核留给适当服务。

00:40:41.568 --> 00:40:57.408
Prone positioning and pressure on the back, chest or neck can impair ventilation. If a patient is restricted by any means, maintain access to the face and breathing, keep the position as safe as possible and summon authorized help.
俯卧以及背部、胸部或颈部受压会妨碍通气。患者受到任何限制时，应保持面部与呼吸可观察，尽可能维持安全体位，并请求授权人员支援。

00:40:57.408 --> 00:41:15.840
The saved school outline specifies q5min vital signs and respiratory monitoring as a station memory target. It is not an all-purpose safe monitoring interval. Follow current protocol, maintain observation appropriate to the risk and escalate any deterioration immediately.
学校保存的纲要把每5分钟生命体征及呼吸监测列为站点记忆目标，但不是通用安全监测间隔。临床应遵循现行规程、按风险充分观察，并立即升级处置任何恶化。

00:41:15.840 --> 00:41:46.176
The second school preparation case begins with police-applied prone restraint, not just a noisy scene. For an original transfer round, an adult outside a venue is hot and struggling while lying face down; a bystander reports pressure over the upper back. Explain the immediate ventilation concern to the responsible officers and coordinate prompt correction of the dangerous position and pressure with trained personnel, while maintaining scene safety and airway access.
学校第二个准备案例一开始就有警方施加的俯卧约束，而不只是嘈杂现场。原创迁移排练中，一名场馆外成年人发热、挣扎并面朝下躺着；旁观者报告其上背部受压。应向负责警员说明即时通气担忧，协调受训人员迅速纠正危险体位及压力，同时保持现场安全及气道可接近。

00:41:46.176 --> 00:42:13.872
Keep the source distinction explicit. The school calls for an immediate stop to prone or hog-tied danger. The current public G01 says three-quarter-prone if possible when law enforcement has applied restraint. That is not permission for fully face-down compression, and neither wording is a hands-on release technique. In class, rehearse the verbal coordination; have the instructor demonstrate any authorized physical skill.
须明确来源区别。学校要求立即停止俯卧或四肢反绑造成的危险。现行公开G01对警方已约束患者写的是“可能时四分之三俯卧”。这不是允许完全面朝下受压，两种表述也都不是徒手解脱技术。课堂应排练口头协调；任何获准身体技能由教师示范。

00:42:13.872 --> 00:42:41.856
Now reveal that the struggling suddenly stops and responses weaken. Interrupt the interview and reassess airway, actual ventilation and circulation immediately; arrange the required support. Record the change and timing. The school five-minute vital-sign target does not authorize waiting. Heat, apparent unusual strength or reduced reaction to pain do not establish a single diagnosis or permit extra force.
接着揭示变化：挣扎突然停止，反应减弱。应中断访谈，立即复评气道、实际通气及循环，并安排所需支持；记录变化及时间。学校每五分钟生命体征目标不允许等待。发热、看似异常有力或疼痛反应减弱，不能确立单一诊断，也不允许加大暴力。

00:42:41.856 --> 00:42:56.712
For an original update, the worker stops speaking and becomes less responsive. Pause the interview and assess the new clinical threat as safely possible. A quiet patient is not automatically an improved patient.
原创变化中，工人停止说话，反应下降。应暂停访谈，并在安全范围内评估新的临床威胁。患者安静下来，不自动等于好转。

00:42:56.712 --> 00:43:12.384
If the person is restricted by another agency, communicate the immediate airway and breathing concern, maintain safe access and obtain appropriate assistance. Do not apply an untrained release or restraint technique as a classroom improvisation.
若本人被其他机构限制，应沟通即时气道及呼吸担忧、保持安全接近，并取得适当协助。不能在课堂上临时发明未经训练的解除或约束手法。

00:43:12.384 --> 00:43:26.424
The school five-minute vital-sign target remains a recall item, not a wait instruction. Check a change when it occurs, and continue the required physiological monitoring rather than using a behavioural score as a substitute.
学校每5分钟生命体征目标仍是记忆事项，不是等待指令。变化发生时就应检查，并继续所需生理监测，不能用行为评分替代。

00:43:26.424 --> 00:43:40.896
Tell the receiving clinician what changed, when, and what happened around the change. Distinguish medication known to have been administered from an assumption based on drowsiness. Document the actual response and unresolved risk.
告知接收人员改变了什么、何时改变及前后发生什么。要区分确实已给药与仅因嗜睡而猜测用药。记录真实反应及未解决风险。

00:43:40.896 --> 00:43:54.720
Chemical sedation is not a routine PCP action and this lesson supplies no drug dose or administration sequence. The current BCEHS G01 pathway distinguishes interventions by provider level.
药物镇静不是PCP常规行动，本课不提供药物剂量或给药流程。BCEHS现行G01按执业层级区分干预。

00:43:54.720 --> 00:44:08.736
A calm appearance after medication is not proof of stability. A trained authorized provider must monitor for respiratory depression, airway compromise, hypotension and worsening illness according to protocol.
给药后看起来平静不代表稳定。受训授权人员必须依规程监测呼吸抑制、气道受损、低血压及疾病恶化。

00:44:08.736 --> 00:44:42.000
G03 makes interfacility transfer a planned clinical encounter. Confirm identity, obtain a meaningful sending-team handover and supporting documents, compare the current assessment with the pre-transport risk assessment, and review the individualized transport plan. Check staff, equipment, escort and family arrangements against actual risk and space. A patient who received medication before departure needs assessment of its effect, not an assumption that the paperwork guarantees stability.
G03把转院视为有计划的临床接触。须确认身份，取得转出团队有意义交接及支持文件，把当前评估与转运前风险评估比较，并核查个体化转运计划。人员、器材、陪护及家属安排应符合实际风险与空间。离院前已用药者需要评估效果，不能以文件齐全就默认稳定。

00:44:42.000 --> 00:45:15.552
The current G03 PCP branch permits medication during transport only as maintenance of therapy described in an individualized transport plan that fits PCP scope; CliniCall must confirm that plan. This is not a blanket ban on every medication associated with sedation, but neither is it permission to start independent field chemical restraint. If the patient, safety or transport needs no longer match the plan, seek re-conference and the appropriate resource rather than stretching the original authorization.
现行G03的PCP分支允许转运途中按个体化转运计划维持治疗，前提是该计划符合PCP范围，并须经CliniCall确认。这不是一概禁止所有与镇静有关药物，但也不允许独立启动现场药物约束。若患者、安全或转运需求已不符合计划，应重新会商并取得适当资源，不能扩大解释原授权。

00:45:15.552 --> 00:45:25.824
A person with advanced illness asks for help with new severe breathlessness at home. A partner says the patient has a no-CPR form and should not be transported.
一位晚期疾病患者在家出现新的严重呼吸困难并求助。伴侣说患者有不复苏表格，因此不应转运。

00:45:25.824 --> 00:45:43.872
Assess the acute change and the patient’s wishes directly. Verify applicable documentation using the current BCEHS pathway. A no-CPR instruction does not mean no assessment, symptom relief or other care, and it does not independently decide transport.
应直接评估急性变化并询问患者意愿。依BCEHS现行流程核实适用文件。不复苏指示不等于不评估、不给症状缓解或不提供其他照护，也不能单独决定是否转运。

00:45:43.872 --> 00:46:17.808
Delirium is an acute, fluctuating change in attention and awareness from the individual baseline. Hyperactive, hypoactive and mixed forms explain why both agitation and unusual withdrawal can matter. Sleep-cycle, cognition or perception may also change. Do not label a newly quiet, sleepy person comfortable without assessment. P02 says delirium near the end of life still deserves recognition and relief, rather than being dismissed as a normal inevitability.
谵妄是注意与觉察相对个人基线的急性、波动改变。活动增多、活动减少及混合型解释了为何躁动与异常退缩都重要；睡眠节律、认知或感知也可变化。新安静嗜睡者不能未经评估就标为舒适。P02强调临终谵妄仍需识别和缓解，不能当成正常且无法避免而忽略。

00:46:17.808 --> 00:46:53.160
Look for contributors that match the person and goals: infection, hypoxia, organ failure, metabolic disturbance, dehydration, withdrawal, poorly controlled pain, sleep loss, constipation, urinary retention and an unfamiliar environment. Reduce avoidable stimulation and provide reassuring familiar contact when helpful. Restraint can worsen delirium. A behavior score describes arousal but does not determine the cause or replace breathing, perfusion and a focused assessment.
应按患者及目标寻找相关因素：感染、缺氧、器官衰竭、代谢异常、脱水、戒断、疼痛控制不佳、缺觉、便秘、尿潴留及陌生环境。可减少不必要刺激，适当时提供安心且熟悉的接触。约束可使谵妄加重；行为评分描述唤醒程度，却不确定病因，也不能替代呼吸、灌注及重点评估。

00:46:53.160 --> 00:47:23.256
Grief is a personal response to loss; mourning is its outward, social or ritual expression; bereavement refers to having experienced a death-related loss. These terms overlap without being identical. A person may grieve a lost role, health, independence, relationship or expected future before anyone dies. A quiet expression does not establish absence of grief, and visible tears do not determine its severity.
Grief是对失去的个人哀伤反应，mourning是外在、社会或仪式性表达，bereavement指经历与死亡相关的丧失。这些词相关但不相同。没有人死亡之前，人也可能因角色、健康、独立、关系或预期未来的失去而哀伤。安静不证明没有哀伤，明显流泪也不决定严重程度。

00:47:23.256 --> 00:47:55.968
The five familiar labels are denial, anger, bargaining, depression and acceptance. The actual source figure shows both continuum and random paths, and the narrative allows repetition and skipped labels. Contemporary grief guidance does not establish one mandatory stage sequence or deadline. The word depression in this model is not automatically a diagnosis of major depressive disorder. Acceptance need not mean approval, forgetting or an absence of distress.
常见五个标签为否认、愤怒、讨价还价、低落及接受。实际来源图同时显示连续和随机路径，正文也允许重复和跳过。现行哀伤指导并不确立必须遵循的阶段顺序或期限。模型中的depression不自动等于重性抑郁障碍诊断。接受也不必意味着赞同、忘记或不再痛苦。

00:47:55.968 --> 00:48:28.752
The chapter’s chronic, delayed, exaggerated and masked categories describe patterns sometimes called complicated or dysfunctional grief. They are not field diagnoses or a universal clock. Ask about persistent suffering, daily function, supports and danger; qualified assessment must distinguish grief, depression, trauma and other illness. The named rating tools, including grief inventories and depression scales, are not interchangeable PCP diagnostic instruments.
本章慢性、延迟、夸大及掩饰类别，描述有时称为复杂或功能失调哀伤的模式。它们不是现场诊断，也不是统一时钟。应询问持续痛苦、日常功能、支持和危险；合资格评估须区分哀伤、抑郁、创伤及其他疾病。文中哀伤量表和抑郁量表等工具，不是可互换的PCP诊断仪器。

00:48:28.752 --> 00:48:43.416
Return to the person with advanced illness and new breathlessness. Ask directly what help they want now. Staying with a partner may be an important goal, but it does not remove the need to assess the change and available relief.
回到晚期疾病且新发呼吸困难的患者。应直接询问现在希望得到什么帮助。与伴侣在一起可能是重要目标，却不免除评估变化及可用缓解措施。

00:48:43.416 --> 00:48:58.392
Ask permission to review the relevant care document and clarify what it actually directs. The presence of a MOST form is not itself a particular resuscitation instruction; read the applicable order instead of accepting a label.
征得许可后查看相关照护文件，并澄清其实际指示。存在MOST表格本身，不等于某种特定复苏指示；应阅读适用医嘱，而非接受标签。

00:48:58.392 --> 00:49:15.624
Use a comfort-focused approach while assessment and coordination continue. When appropriate, simple positioning, a calmer environment and airflow may help; use current symptom guidance and the patient’s response, not a fixed comfort checklist for everyone.
继续评估与协调时，可采取舒适导向方式。适当时，简单体位调整、较平静环境及空气流动可能有帮助；应依现行症状指导及患者反应，而非对所有人套固定清单。

00:49:15.624 --> 00:49:26.592
Contact the relevant care team or consultation route with the patient’s goals and clinical findings. Do not promise home management before an actual workable plan is established.
向相关照护团队或咨询渠道沟通患者目标及临床发现。在建立真正可落实的计划前，不能承诺一定能居家处理。

00:49:26.592 --> 00:49:55.320
Apply the assigned ethics chapter to the palliative station. Autonomy asks whose informed decision is being made. Beneficence and nonmaleficence require comparison of benefit and harm in this person's circumstances. Justice asks whether barriers have prevented fair participation, and fidelity requires honest commitments. Naming all five principles is not a justified plan unless you explain how they change the available actions.
把指定伦理章节用到姑息站点：自主问谁在作知情决定；行善与不伤害要求结合本人处境比较收益伤害；公正问障碍是否影响公平参与；忠实要求诚实承诺。只列五个原则不等于合理计划，必须解释它们怎样改变可用行动。

00:49:55.320 --> 00:50:24.000
Recognize the clinical and ethical cues, identify the actual conflict, compare feasible alternatives and obtain the appropriate decision before acting. Then evaluate the response. Do not obey an unclear instruction blindly, invent a treatment outside your role or postpone immediate support while filling an ethics table. Record the reasoning, consultation, action and reassessment trigger so another clinician can follow the decision.
识别临床伦理线索、明确真实冲突、比较可执行替代方案，取得恰当决定后行动，再评价效果。不能盲从含糊指示、越职责编治疗，也不能为了填伦理表推迟即时支持。记录理由、咨询、行动及复评触发点，让下一临床者能理解决定。

00:50:24.000 --> 00:50:54.072
In this original variation, a sixty-eight-year-old artist with serious lung disease asks to speak privately and receive relief before deciding about travel. A sibling requests every detail and produces a financial power of attorney. Assess immediate needs while giving the person an accessible opportunity to explain what matters. Family worry deserves support, but does not automatically displace a capable patient or permit unrestricted disclosure.
本原创变式中，六十八岁严重肺病艺术家希望私下谈话、先缓解再决定出行。手足要求全部细节并出示财务授权书。评估即时需要的同时，让本人能理解并表达重视事项。家属担心值得支持，但不自动取代有能力患者，也不允许无限披露。

00:50:54.072 --> 00:51:25.080
The American durable-power-of-attorney description is not the BC rule. A BC enduring power of attorney concerns financial and legal affairs, not health-care consent merely because the person named is present. Verify the actual document and any relevant health-care authority through the applicable process. Keep the present patient decision, permission to share information and substitute authority as separate questions; do not settle all three from a family title.
美国持久授权描述不是BC规则。BC持久财务授权涉及财务法律，不能因为被指定人到场就获得医疗同意权。按适用流程核实真实文件及相关医疗权限。本人当下决定、信息分享许可及替代权限是三个问题，不能用一个家属称谓全部定论。

00:51:25.080 --> 00:51:54.456
The assigned source sometimes restricts palliation to failed curative treatment. Keep the broader correction visible: palliative care can be integrated early during serious illness and addresses more than physical pain. An expected change is not a reliable countdown, and quietness is not proof of comfort. Assess what the artist reports, the breathing pattern and the actual response to authorized support rather than assuming all symptoms belong to dying.
指定来源有时把姑息限于治愈失败，要保留更宽的纠正：严重疾病过程中可早期整合姑息，也不仅处理身体痛。可能变化不是可靠倒计时，安静不证明舒适。评估艺术家自述、呼吸模式及授权支持后的真实反应，不假定一切症状都属临终。

00:51:54.456 --> 00:52:19.056
Explain the relevant options without using your personal beliefs to steer the answer. Reduce information overload, address hearing and language needs and ask the person to explain the plan in their own words. Teach-back checks your explanation, not whether the patient deserves a choice. Agree on what can be shared with the sibling, what they can safely help with and what must be passed to the responsible care team.
解释相关选项，不用个人信念引导答案。减少信息过载、处理听力语言需要，请本人用自己的话说计划。复述检查自己的说明，不是判断患者是否配有选择。约定可向手足分享什么、其能安全协助什么，以及何事必须传给负责团队。

00:52:19.056 --> 00:52:47.280
Before describing a plan as complete, check whether the actual team accepted follow-up and whether the chosen support person is willing and able to carry out the agreed role. A voicemail is not an accepted handover, and an unavailable hospice team is not a universal instruction never to seek emergency help. Document the artist's own decision, verified authority, observed response, unresolved concern and the feasible fallback.
称计划完成前，检查真实团队是否接收后续，所选支持者是否愿意且能做约定角色。留言不是已接收交接，临终团队不可用也不表示永不求急救。记录艺术家自己决定、已核实权限、观察反应、未解担忧及可执行备用方案。

00:52:47.280 --> 00:53:16.200
Support realistic hope and the person's preferred cultural or spiritual practices without prescribing a grief stage or copying a religion table onto an individual. After the encounter, reflect on the strain, seek appropriate support and protect confidentiality. Ethical consultation and colleague support help you reason; they do not transfer responsibility, replace urgent care or require the patient to accept your own beliefs about a good death.
支持现实希望及本人文化灵性偏好，不规定哀伤阶段，也不把宗教表套给个人。接触后反思负担、寻求恰当支持并保护隐私。伦理咨询同事支持帮助推理，不转移责任、不代替紧急照护，也不要求本人接受你对善终的信念。

00:53:16.200 --> 00:53:53.064
Group the nitrous exclusions by mechanism. Gas-filled spaces can expand: pneumothorax, air embolism, decompression illness and gross abdominal distension matter. Current guidance also lists bullous emphysema. Inability to cooperate or altered awareness defeats safe self-administration; inhalation injury and recent nitroglycerin within five minutes are additional listed exclusions. The printed card puts abdominal distension among cautions, while the current monograph lists gross distension as a contraindication. Preserve that distinction.
可按机制组织一氧化二氮排除项。含气空间可扩张，气胸、气栓、减压病及明显腹胀因此重要；现行指导还列大疱性肺气肿。不能配合或意识改变破坏安全自行吸入，吸入性损伤及五分钟内用硝酸甘油是其他所列排除项。印刷卡把腹胀放注意项，现行专论则把明显腹胀列禁忌，应保留区别。

00:53:53.064 --> 00:54:23.520
Self-administered is a safety condition, not a command to press the interface onto a drowsy patient. Explain the method and expected sensations, observe pain and function alongside awareness, breathing, perfusion and adverse effects, and record what actually happened. Keep environmental ventilation and patient ventilation separate: an exhaust fan reduces occupational exposure, but does not ventilate the lungs of an inadequately breathing patient.
自行吸入是一项安全条件，不是把接口按在嗜睡患者脸上的指令。应解释方法及可能感受，同时观察疼痛功能、意识、呼吸、灌注和不良效应，并记录实际情况。须区分环境通风与患者通气：排风扇减少职业暴露，却不能替呼吸不足者通气。

00:54:23.520 --> 00:54:57.552
The printed CHECK list is internally inconsistent: it omits the established malignant-hyperthermia item in the mnemonic list and ends with adult dosages. British Columbia Emergency Health Services expands CHECK as cardiac instability or respiratory depression, hypersensitivity, established malignant hyperthermia, consciousness and kidneys. This does not replace the separate full contraindication list. A neat mnemonic is useful only if it preserves the actual exclusion, not if it makes a missing risk disappear.
印刷CHECK列表内部不一致：口诀项漏掉已确诊恶性高热，末项写成人剂量。BCEHS现行展开为循环不稳定或呼吸抑制、超敏、已确诊恶性高热、意识及肾脏。这也不替代另列完整禁忌。口诀只有保留真实排除项才有用，不能因排列好看就让遗漏风险消失。

00:54:57.552 --> 00:55:31.968
Keep three ceilings distinct. The source and current adult pathway give three milliliters, with a repeat after twenty minutes and a six-milliliter total; current guidance further limits a patient to six milliliters in twenty-four hours and fifteen over a week. Provider exposure is a different limit: three doses, nine milliliters total in twenty-four hours. Do not give a patient nine because that is the responder exposure limit, or treat a weekly maximum as an amount to finish. Record earlier doses and the time.
应区分三类上限。来源及现行成人路径为3 mL，二十分钟后可重复，总量6 mL；现行指导进一步限定患者二十四小时6 mL、一周15 mL。工作人员暴露是另一上限：二十四小时三剂、总9 mL。不能因人员暴露上限而给患者9 mL，也不能把周上限当应完成量。须记录已用量及时间。

00:55:31.968 --> 00:56:10.464
Breakthrough pain is a temporary worsening on a background of otherwise reasonably controlled pain. A prescribed rescue dose supplements rather than automatically replaces the regular schedule. Keep the exact medicine, route, formulation, regular twenty-four-hour amount and every rescue administration separate. The source total daily dose includes regular plus breakthrough use; that is not necessarily the same denominator as total regular daily dose. Repeated rescue use calls for reassessment and an authorized plan review, not endless unsupervised escalation.
突破痛是在其他时间控制尚可背景下的短暂加重。处方救援剂量用于补充，不自动替代固定时间表。须分别记录准确药物、途径、剂型、二十四小时固定量及每次救援给药。来源总日量含固定加突破用量，不一定等于固定日总量这个分母。反复救援需复评及授权计划复核，不能无监督不断加量。

00:56:10.464 --> 00:56:51.000
The P03 text itself changes the breakthrough denominator: one passage uses ten percent of the regular daily opioid amount, while the titration passage says ten percent of the new regular dose after dividing the daily total by six. These are not equivalent. For an original arithmetic illustration, ten percent of one hundred twenty is twelve, but ten percent of one hundred twenty divided by six is two. This exposes a sixfold difference. This illustration is not a patient prescription. Verify the actual prescribed regimen and obtain clarification rather than silently choosing one interpretation.
P03本身改变了突破剂量分母：一段用固定阿片日量的10%，滴定段却写把日总量除以六后，新固定单次剂量的10%。两者不等价。原创纯算术例：120的10%是12，而120除以六后再取10%是2，相差六倍。这里暴露差异，不是在选择患者剂量。须核实真实处方方案并澄清，不能悄悄任选解释。

00:56:51.000 --> 00:57:02.136
The partner now says the document is not available and only remembers that the patient did not want CPR. Record this as a reported preference, not as a form you have inspected.
伴侣现在说拿不到文件，只记得患者不希望CPR。应把它记为所报告偏好，而不是已经查看过的表格。

00:57:02.136 --> 00:57:19.200
P07 requires CliniCall guidance when clear resuscitation documentation is unavailable, including a verbal order claim. Do not invent an arrest decision from the palliative label or a remembered document; communicate the actual uncertainty promptly.
P07要求在明确复苏文件不可用时取得CliniCall指导，包括只有口头医嘱说法的情况。不能由姑息标签或记忆中的文件编造心搏骤停决定；应及时沟通真实不确定性。

00:57:19.200 --> 00:57:33.576
In this breathing patient, continue appropriate assessment and symptom care while clarification occurs. A no-CPR instruction concerns resuscitation, not a general instruction to stop every helpful action.
本例患者仍在呼吸，澄清期间应继续适当评估及症状照护。不复苏指示针对复苏，不是停止全部有益行动的一般命令。

00:57:33.576 --> 00:57:49.680
If the clinical situation changes, use the current resuscitation, goals-of-care and consultation pathways for that situation. Do not turn this classroom comparison into independent authority to pronounce death or withhold an unreviewed intervention.
临床情况改变时，应使用适用于当时情境的现行复苏、照护目标及咨询流程。不能把课堂对比当作独立死亡宣告，或不经审查拒绝某项干预的权限。

00:57:49.680 --> 00:58:27.264
Dyspnea is the person’s uncomfortable breathing sensation; it may occur without hypoxemia. Assess the actual effort, speech, responsiveness, circulation, saturation/baseline and possible cause while clarifying relief goals. Appropriate positioning, reassurance and gentle airflow may help. The P04 five-minute airflow trial applies to its nonhypoxic context, not an instruction to wait through inadequate ventilation, collapse or another immediate threat. Reassess the patient’s reported relief and objective state separately.
呼吸困难是本人不舒服的呼吸感受，未必伴低氧血症。澄清缓解目标的同时，应评估真实呼吸功、说话、反应、循环、饱和度及基线和可能病因。适当体位、安抚及轻柔气流可能有帮助。P04五分钟气流试验针对其无低氧背景，不允许在通气不足、倒地或其他即时威胁中等待。须分别复评本人缓解感受及客观状态。

00:58:27.264 --> 00:59:04.152
Noisy secretions can upset a family without proving the patient is distressed. Assess the person: facial tension, effort, responsiveness, airway and goals matter more than sound alone. P06 favors suitable side-lying/head elevation and allows gentle anterior suction for accessible oral secretions, not routine deep suction to silence every rattle. Oxygen for actual hypoxia is a different question from oxygen to remove a sound. Explain what you see and what a comfort intervention is intended to change.
嘈杂分泌物可使家属难受，却不证明患者痛苦。应评估本人，表情紧张、呼吸功、反应、气道及目标比声音本身更重要。P06倾向适当侧卧和抬高头部，可对可及口腔分泌物轻柔前部吸引，不是为消除每次喉鸣而常规深吸引。真实低氧时供氧，不同于为消除声音供氧。应解释所见及舒适干预希望改变什么。

00:59:04.152 --> 00:59:37.008
Table 36.4 organizes possible dying-related changes by system. Reduced perfusion may appear as cool or mottled skin and a changing pulse or pressure; breathing can become irregular, effortful or noisy as cough and secretion clearance change. These findings are not a fixed early-middle-late timetable, nor a substitute for assessing a new treatable problem. Abnormal or agonal breathing requires the real emergency and goals-of-care decision, not a stage label.
表36.4按系统整理可能的濒死变化。灌注下降可表现为皮肤凉或花斑，以及脉搏或血压变化；随着咳嗽和分泌物清除改变，呼吸可不规则、费力或有声。这些不是固定早中晚时间表，也不能替代对新可治疗问题的评估。异常或濒死喘息须进入真实急救及照护目标决策，不能仅贴阶段标签。

00:59:37.008 --> 01:00:09.240
Reduced intake can be upsetting to caregivers who associate food with care. Explain the observed swallowing and comfort needs without promising that fluids will reverse dying. Offer mouth and lip care and, where desired and safe, assistance with suitable sips or food. Do not force intake into someone who cannot swallow safely. Clinically assisted hydration requires individual assessment of possible benefit and harm; neither always give fluids nor never give fluids is the lesson.
摄入减少可能令把食物视为照护的家属痛苦。应解释观察到的吞咽和舒适需要，不承诺补液能逆转濒死。可提供口腔及唇部照护，并在本人希望且安全时协助适当小口饮水或进食。不能强迫不能安全吞咽者摄入。医疗辅助补液须个体化评估获益与伤害，本课不是“总要补液”或“一律不补液”。

01:00:09.240 --> 01:00:23.568
Palliative guidance supports care at home when it fits the person’s wishes and the actual situation. It does not require transport for every symptom, and it does not guarantee that every new crisis can be managed at home.
当符合本人意愿及实际情况时，姑息指导支持居家照护。它不要求每个症状都转运，也不保证每次新危机都能居家处理。

01:00:23.568 --> 01:00:38.904
Review the observed symptom response, remaining distress and the accepted follow-up plan. If symptoms remain uncontrolled or a safe arrangement is unavailable, explain the available options and obtain the indicated clinical decision.
复查观察到的症状反应、剩余痛苦及已接收后续计划。若症状仍未控制，或无法建立安全安排，应解释可用选项，并取得所需临床决定。

01:00:38.904 --> 01:00:52.584
Check whether the chosen support person can and wants to perform the agreed role. Family presence is not automatic evidence of available care, and a phone message is not confirmation that the home team will attend.
确认所选支持者能否且是否愿意承担约定角色。家属在场不自动证明可提供照护，电话留言也不证明居家团队会到场。

01:00:52.584 --> 01:01:04.848
Use teach-back for the practical next step and contingency, then hand over responsibility clearly. Record what is agreed, what remains uncertain and who will respond if the plan fails.
对实际下一步及应变安排使用复述确认，再清楚交接责任。记录已同意事项、剩余不确定性，以及计划失败时由谁回应。

01:01:04.848 --> 01:01:41.208
For authorized teaching or simulation, explain the purpose and contact, agree on consent/privacy and the patient preferred participation, and offer supported self-administration when appropriate. Prepare clean gloves, the correct medication, water-soluble lubricant and supplies. The source adult position is left side-lying with the upper leg flexed, with minimal necessary exposure and protected linens. A comfortable position and relaxation reduce avoidable trauma; they do not remove the need to reassess consent or contraindications.
在获授权教学或模拟中，应解释目的及接触，确认同意、隐私和患者希望的参与方式；适当时支持自行给药。准备洁净手套、正确药物、水溶性润滑及用品。来源成人体位为左侧卧、上腿屈曲，仅暴露必要部位并保护床单。舒适体位及放松可减少不必要创伤，但不免除复核同意及禁忌。

01:01:41.208 --> 01:02:16.656
The source sequence is inspection, removal of the wrapper, water-soluble lubrication, gentle insertion toward the umbilicus while the patient relaxes, and placement against rectal mucosa rather than stool. Its adult example is about five centimeters beyond the anal sphincter; that is a source technique, not a universal depth for every age, formulation or device. Do not force against a clenched sphincter or substitute petroleum lubricant without product approval. Actual product instructions and the supervised procedure control the method.
来源顺序为检查、去包装、水溶性润滑，在患者放松时轻柔向脐方向置入，并使药接触直肠黏膜而不是粪便。成人例子为肛门括约肌以里约5 cm，这是来源技术，不是所有年龄、剂型和器材的通用深度。不能强推紧闭括约肌，也不能未经产品认可改用石油类润滑。真实产品说明及监督操作决定方法。

01:02:16.656 --> 01:02:46.584
The source preparation includes opportunity to empty the bladder, explanation and privacy, a comfortable supine position with knees flexed, minimal exposure, clean gloves and assessment for discharge, itching or burning. Verify that the patient understands the proposed contact and wishes to continue. Adapt positioning and assistance to mobility, pain and dignity; a printed position is not an instruction to restrain or force a person into it.
来源准备包括可先排空膀胱、解释及隐私、舒适仰卧屈膝、最小暴露、洁净手套，以及评估分泌物、瘙痒或灼热。须确认患者理解拟进行接触并愿意继续。体位和协助应按活动能力、疼痛及尊严调整，印刷体位不是约束或强迫摆位的指令。

01:02:46.584 --> 01:03:21.792
The source removes packaging, uses water-soluble lubricant for the specified suppository, and gently places it along the posterior vaginal wall; its adult manual example is eight-to-ten centimeters. An applicator follows its own manufacturer directions. This is an explanation of the nursing example, not one depth or lubricant rule for every patient/product. Afterward provide comfort, remove excess lubricant as appropriate, discard supplies, clean hands and document tolerance and relevant findings.
来源去包装，对所述栓剂使用水溶性润滑，并轻柔沿阴道后壁放置；成人手工示例为8至10 cm。施药器须按自身厂家说明。这是在解释护理例子，不是所有患者或产品都同一深度和润滑规则。之后按需保持舒适、除去多余润滑，处理用品、清洁双手，并记耐受及相关发现。

01:03:21.792 --> 01:04:02.352
Current British Columbia Emergency Health Services procedure P R twenty-four is headed ACP and higher and requires CliniCall before establishing or using the medication site. Community-paramedicine pathway four point twenty-one exempts its trained community paramedics from calling before insertion, within the service request and care plan; it does not grant all PCPs independent medication authority. For a PCP student, distinguish observing, explaining, supervised rehearsal and assisting within actual authorization from independently inserting or administering. A school reading label alone does not change that distinction.
BCEHS现行PR24标题为ACP及以上，要求建立或经该点给药前咨询CliniCall。社区辅助医疗4.21路径免除该路径下受训社区辅助医务人员在置入前的致电要求，仍须在服务请求及照护计划内进行；这不授予全部PCP独立给药权限。PCP学生须区分观察、解释、监督练习及真实授权内协助，与独立置入给药。学校阅读标签不会改变此区别。

01:04:02.352 --> 01:04:36.624
PR24 organizes preparation around consent/plan, clean hands and equipment, a healthy accessible site, skin antisepsis allowed to dry, and the correct catheter/connector. Its selected device example primes with medication, including an additional zero point four milliliters for that set and connector; it is not an instruction to add that volume to every device or flush any existing line. Prime/dead-space volume, concentration and the ordered patient amount are different quantities.
PR24准备围绕同意与计划、洁净手和器材、健康可及部位、皮肤消毒后待干，以及正确导管接头。其指定器材例子用药液预充，该套管路接头另需0.4 mL；这不是每种器材都加此体积或冲洗任何既存管路的指令。预充死腔体积、浓度及医嘱患者用量是不同量。

01:04:36.624 --> 01:05:07.656
Original comfort-care case: a patient cannot swallow the usual tablet, is newly breathless and has a painful swollen site under a dressing. A relative calls the device a butterfly and asks you to flush it and give the usual medicine another way. Explain the immediate assessment, what identity/medication/plan facts are missing, and how to obtain appropriate help. The word palliative does not make hypoxia, pain or a damaged medication site unimportant.
原创舒适照护病例：患者吞不下平时片剂，新发气短，敷料下部位痛肿。亲属称其蝶形针，要求冲管并换途径给平时药。请解释即时评估、缺少哪些身份药物及计划事实，以及如何取得适当支援。姑息二字不会让缺氧、疼痛或异常给药点变得不重要。

01:05:07.656 --> 01:05:44.520
Worked reasoning: assess airway, breathing, circulation, symptoms and goals; identify the real device and site, review the medication record and obtain the relevant clinician/consultation support. Do not crush a tablet into an unverified route or flush an unknown medication-filled set. Explain what you can do now for comfort and safety, preserve privacy and document the observed problem, actual actions and response. A clear handover connects route safety with compassionate care rather than treating them as competing priorities.
推理示范：评估气道、呼吸、循环、症状及目标，识别真实器材部位，核对给药记录并取得相应临床或咨询支持。不能把片剂碾碎放入未核实途径，也不能冲洗不明含药套件。应解释此刻能为舒适和安全做什么、保护隐私，记录所见问题、真实行动及反应。清楚交接把途径安全与有同理心照护相连，而非互相竞争。

01:05:44.520 --> 01:06:00.024
Medical assistance in dying is a distinct, regulated process. Under current federal information, assessment and provision are performed by physicians or nurse practitioners; it is not limited to people whose death is reasonably foreseeable.
医疗协助死亡是独立且受监管的流程。按联邦现行信息，评估和实施由医生或执业护士负责；资格并不限于死亡可合理预见者。

01:06:00.024 --> 01:06:22.056
As of October 2026, eligibility where mental illness is the sole underlying condition remains excluded until March 17, 2027. Responders should not assess eligibility, administer MAiD medication or rely on an older BCEHS page for current legal details; follow current EMALB and service policy.
截至2026年10月，若精神疾病是唯一基础病因，资格仍被排除至2027年3月17日。急救人员不得评估资格或实施MAiD给药，也不应依据旧版BCEHS网页判断现行法律细节；应遵循EMALB及服务现行政策。

01:06:22.056 --> 01:06:34.920
A person asking about MAiD is not automatically refusing every assessment or symptom treatment. Ask what the current request means and distinguish an information request from an urgent medical change.
询问MAiD的人，不自动等于拒绝全部评估或症状治疗。应询问当前请求的含义，区分信息请求与紧急医学变化。

01:06:34.920 --> 01:06:48.264
The dated federal eligibility note in the preceding slide is not a student eligibility checklist. Recognize that qualified clinicians govern that process; do not offer a conclusion about whether this patient qualifies.
前页带日期的联邦资格说明，不是学生资格核对表。应认识到该流程由合资格临床人员负责，不能对这位患者是否符合资格作结论。

01:06:48.264 --> 01:07:03.576
If called during an unexpected deterioration, communicate the confirmed event, current findings, relevant documents and known treating-team plan. Do not assume that the word MAiD supplies an order or explains an unknown medication event.
若在意外恶化时被呼叫，应沟通已确认事件、当前发现、相关文件及已知治疗团队计划。不能假设MAiD这个词本身提供医嘱，或解释未知用药事件。

01:07:03.576 --> 01:07:19.512
Maintain a respectful, nonjudgmental interaction and obtain current clinical direction for the actual problem. This is role recognition and communication, not training to provide MAiD or an instruction to improvise medication assistance.
应维持尊重、不评判的互动，并就实际问题取得现行临床指导。这是角色识别及沟通，不是MAiD实施培训，也不指示临时安排给药协助。

01:07:19.512 --> 01:07:50.208
Distinguish symptom-focused palliative treatment from MAiD by the intended intervention and authorized process, not by whether a medicine can also cause sedation. MAiD includes clinician administration and the separate prescribed/provided self-administration method; qualified physicians or nurse practitioners assess eligibility and provide it under the legal framework. A paramedic listening to a question or supporting an authorized transport is not thereby an assessor or provider of MAiD.
应按干预目的及授权流程区分症状导向姑息治疗与MAiD，不能只看某药是否也可造成镇静。MAiD包括临床人员给药及另种处方提供后本人自服方式，由符合资格的医生或执业护士依法评估资格及提供。辅助医务人员听取问题或支持授权转运，并不会因此成为MAiD评估或实施者。

01:07:50.208 --> 01:08:28.080
The Emergency Medical Assistants Licensing Board policy twenty nineteen dash zero one applies to qualified EMAs licensed or endorsed to initiate intravenous lines. It allows an ordered IV start for MAiD from a physician or nurse practitioner, but prohibits EMA administration of MAiD medication in any circumstance. Licence, training, the order and service policy still matter. Its 2026 change-index entry updates contact information, not this authority. The policy body, rather than merely its index title, was reviewed.
实际EMALB2019-01政策适用于获执照或加项、具备建立静脉通路资格的EMA。其允许依据医生或执业护士医嘱为MAiD建立静脉通路，但禁止EMA在任何情况下给MAiD药。执照、培训、医嘱及机构政策仍重要。其2026年变更记录更新联系方式，并未改变权限。本次核查的是政策正文，不只是索引标题。

01:08:28.080 --> 01:08:59.352
After death, dignity, family support, identity, belongings, cultural wishes and the appropriate notification pathway still matter. Algor mortis means postmortem cooling. Rigor mortis means stiffening. Lividity means dependent blood pooling. Pallor means paleness. The source’s statement that skin develops passive euthanasia is a wording error, not a physical sign. These signs cannot, by themselves, determine an exact time or cause of death.
死亡之后，尊严、家属支持、身份、物品、文化意愿及适当通知流程仍重要。Algor mortis指尸冷，rigor mortis指尸僵，lividity指低位血液淤积产生的尸斑，pallor指苍白。来源写皮肤出现“passive euthanasia”是措辞错误，不是体征。这些体征本身不能确定准确死亡时间或死因。

01:08:59.352 --> 01:09:31.992
The hospital nursing description of washing, removing tubes or preparing viewing is not a blanket prehospital instruction. In a potentially reportable BC death, protect the body, immediate environment and relevant evidence, follow the service and coroner requirements and obtain required authorization before alteration. Explain constraints compassionately and preserve privacy. Do not remove lines merely for tidiness. Do not clean the scene or assume that a funeral transfer is authorized.
医院护理中清洁、拔管或准备瞻仰的描述，不是一概适用的院前指示。BC可能须报告的死亡，应保护遗体、直接环境及相关证据，遵循机构和验尸官要求，并在改变前取得所需授权。须体恤地解释限制并保护隐私。不能仅为整洁拔除管路，也不能清理现场或默认殡葬转移已获授权。

01:09:31.992 --> 01:09:43.056
Use an observer to note whether the learner explained their role, asked before touch, used plain language, invited the patient’s own account and reassessed when the scene changed.
由观察者记录学员是否说明角色、触碰前征求许可、使用通俗语言、邀请患者表达自身情况，并在现场变化时重新评估。

01:09:43.056 --> 01:10:02.136
For a refusal station, verbalize the decision-specific facts, support provided, risks and options discussed, consultation, documentation and safety-net. For a crisis station, verbalize exit, medical differential, monitoring plan and stop point.
拒绝站点应口述针对该决定的事实、提供的支持、讨论的风险与选项、咨询、记录及安全网。危机站点应口述撤离路线、医学鉴别、监测计划及停止行动条件。

01:10:02.136 --> 01:10:16.704
A useful handover separates the patient’s words from your observations. Include changes over time, the capacity or refusal discussion when relevant, the patient’s goal, applicable documents and any safety concerns.
有用交接应把患者原话与直接观察分开。相关时包括时间变化、决定能力或拒绝讨论、患者目标、适用文件及安全担忧。

01:10:16.704 --> 01:10:46.272
Use SBAR to organize a consultation request. For a current BCEHS care transition, A zero three specifies ATMIST AMBO. Carry forward the actual findings, trend, patient goals, relevant consent discussion and safety concern in the appropriate format. Name the next task and confirm who accepted responsibility. Do not leave only an unexplained not-for-hospital label or an incomplete monitoring plan.
可用SBAR组织咨询请求；现行BCEHS照护责任交接由A03规定使用ATMIST AMBO。应以适当格式传递真实发现、趋势、患者目标、相关同意讨论及安全担忧，指出下一任务，并确认谁接受责任。不能只留下未解释的“不送医院”标签或不完整监测计划。

01:10:46.272 --> 01:10:59.808
In the palliative case, begin with new breathlessness and the patient’s goal of relief while remaining with the partner. Do not start and end with not for hospital; that phrase hides the clinical question.
姑息案例交接应从新发呼吸困难，以及患者希望缓解并留在伴侣身边的目标开始。不能只以“不要去医院”开头和结束，因为这会隐藏临床问题。

01:10:59.808 --> 01:11:12.216
Say which document was actually reviewed or which preference was reported, then describe assessment and response. Distinguish a contacted team from a team that has accepted responsibility.
说明实际查看了哪份文件，或哪项偏好来自报告，再描述评估及反应。应区分已联系团队，与已接手责任的团队。

01:11:12.216 --> 01:11:28.632
For the refusal case, carry forward the specific decision, information/support given, observed understanding and the current consultation or plan. For the crisis case, include safety changes and physiological trend, not only the behaviour score.
拒绝案例应交接具体决定、所给信息及支持、观察到的理解，以及当前咨询或计划。危机案例应包括安全变化及生理趋势，不能只有行为分数。

01:11:28.632 --> 01:11:42.624
Ask for acknowledgment of the next responsibility. A handover is complete when the receiving person understands the unresolved concern and the actual next action, not simply when the speaker finishes a mnemonic.
应要求确认下一责任。交接完成的标志，是接收者理解未解决担忧及实际下一行动，而不只是发言者讲完口诀。

01:11:42.624 --> 01:12:13.848
Original transfer round: a patient being moved between facilities has a confirmed maintenance plan and received a medicine at the sending ward. During loading the patient becomes unusually quiet, develops shallow breathing and cannot explain new abdominal pain. A companion wants the next planned medication given immediately and asks to bypass the receiving hospital because a palliative document is in the bag. Identify which assumptions have stopped being safe and which facts you need now.
原创转院排练：患者有已确认维持治疗计划，转出病房已给一种药。装车时，患者异常安静、呼吸浅，无法解释新腹痛。同行者要求立刻给下一次计划药，并因包里有姑息文件而绕过接收医院。请指出哪些假设已不安全，以及现在需要哪些事实。

01:12:13.848 --> 01:12:51.792
Worked reasoning: pause the routine transfer script and assess airway, ventilation, circulation, responsiveness and the new symptom; coordinate appropriate support. Confirm the actual medicine, dose, route, time and response, and re-conference the plan that no longer matches the patient. Verify the document’s real instruction and the person’s goals through the applicable pathway; neither a companion’s request nor a palliative label establishes informed refusal or drug authority. Communicate the change and the agreed next action with explicit ownership.
推理示范：暂停例行转院台词，评估气道、通气、循环、反应及新症状，协调适当支持。核实真实药物、剂量、途径、时间及反应，对已不符合患者情况的计划重新会商。按适用流程核查文件实际指示及本人目标；同行者要求或姑息标签，都不确立知情拒绝或给药权限。交接变化及商定下一步，并明确责任人。

01:12:51.792 --> 01:13:05.136
After a rehearsal, compare the decision path with the evidence available at that moment. A good outcome does not prove that the reasoning was sound, and a difficult outcome does not by itself prove the learner acted badly.
排练后应根据当时可得证据复盘决策路径。结果良好不证明推理一定正确，结果困难也不能单独证明学员做错了。

01:13:05.136 --> 01:13:16.272
Ask for specific instructor feedback on communication, assessment, monitoring and scope. A discussion does not replace a school checkoff or real-world authorization.
应向教师询问沟通、评估、监测及执业范围方面的具体反馈。讨论不能替代学校技能考核或真实执业授权。

01:13:16.272 --> 01:13:27.480
Begin the debrief with the evidence available at the time, including what was not known. Do not award good reasoning only because the observer later revealed a favourable ending.
复盘从当时可得证据开始，包括哪些仍未知。不能仅因观察者后来揭示了好结局，就认定推理良好。

01:13:27.480 --> 01:13:42.504
Choose one concrete repair. If the patient’s refusal was never clarified, repeat the first conversation with a question about the specific proposal. If a quiet patient was assumed stable, repeat the response to that change.
选择一项具体修复。若从未澄清拒绝内容，就以具体提议的问题重做首次对话；若把安静患者假定为稳定，就重做对该变化的回应。

01:13:42.504 --> 01:13:53.640
The observer writes the actual improved action and remaining gap. Keep a useful behaviour as well as one change; confidence alone is not the performance measure.
观察者记录真正改善的行动及剩余缺口。既保留有用行为，也指出一项改变；自信本身不是表现指标。

01:13:53.640 --> 01:14:05.976
Bring unresolved skill or legal-policy questions to supervised teaching. This round creates a practice record and a next learning task, not a declaration that the school station has been passed.
把未解决技能或法律政策问题带回受监督教学。本轮形成练习记录及下一学习任务，不是宣告已通过学校站点。
